{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg23ugTqwHjsoNHe7pQz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For [Cr(NH₃)₆]³⁺ I get **Dq = 2155 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 657 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3400 cm⁻¹**. I worked in the full octahedral d³ ligand-field model, using the ground state ⁴A₂g and the three assigned bands.\n\n**1. Dq from the ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₂g band**\nFor d³ ions this band's energy equals 10Dq exactly, because the ⁴T₂g state has no partner of the same symmetry to mix with.\n10Dq = 21 550 cm⁻¹, so **Dq = 2155 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**2. B from the ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₁g(F) band**\nThe two ⁴T₁g states (from ⁴F and ⁴P) mix through B, which gives:\n\nE(⁴T₁g(F)) = 15Dq + 7.5B − ½·√(225B² − 180B·Dq + 100Dq²)\n\n- Setting this to 28 500 cm⁻¹ with Dq = 2155: 7.5B + 3825 = ½·√(225B² − 387 900B + 4.644×10⁸)\n- Squaring both sides gives 617 400·B = 4.0588×10⁸\n- So **B ≈ 657.4 cm⁻¹**. This is about 64 % of the free-ion Cr³⁺ value (about 1030 cm⁻¹), so the nephelauxetic ratio β ≈ 0.64.\n\n**3. C from the spin-forbidden ⁴A₂g → ²E_g band**\nThe ²E_g energy depends on C as well as B, and its ²E_g state mixes with four other ²E_g configurations. Simple closed formulas are only approximate, so I built the full 120-determinant d³ Hamiltonian (crystal field plus Racah interelectronic repulsion) and diagonalised it numerically.\n\n- I checked the code against the free ion with Dq = 0: it gives ⁴P − ⁴F = 15B and ²G − ⁴F = 4B + 3C, both correct.\n- I then solved all three band conditions together. The fit reproduces 21 550, 28 500 and 15 200 cm⁻¹ exactly, with Dq = 2155.0, B = 657.4 and **C ≈ 3398 cm⁻¹**.\n- This gives C/B ≈ 5.2. A common shortcut assumes C ≈ 4B, which here would put ²E near 12 860 cm⁻¹ instead of the observed 15 200 cm⁻¹. That is why C has to be fitted separately rather than assumed.\n\nThe model also places the other spin-forbidden doublets (from ²G) at about 15 720 cm⁻¹ (²T₁g) and 23 290 cm⁻¹ (²T₂g).\n\n{\"Dq\": 2155, \"B\": 657.4, \"C\": 3398, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Exact d3 octahedral diagonalisation fitted to the 4T2, 4T1(F) and 2E bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1931,"cache_read_input_tokens":5129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1931,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb81be1a-bea6-4f0c-b972-ece67c2c6f6c","uuid":"48f9c74f-94b6-42ac-901e-fb1c37e031b6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T12:46:59.901Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg23uHPqr89SmuVHquGM"}
